ils.yaml (testutils PRD -- primary specification for the differential testing harness)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (testutils use case -- concrete execution path through the differential testing system)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component, DiffTest data structure definition, design decisions DD2 and DD4)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, RunDiffTest function, output comparison logic, normalization hook support\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define the DiffTest struct with fields for command-line arguments, stdin input, environment variables, expected exit code, and expected stdout/stderr -- per the PRD data structure specification and ARCHITECTURE.yaml DiffTest definition\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement a function that executes a Go binary and a reference GNU binary with identical stdin, arguments, and environment, capturing stdout, stderr, and exit code from each\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte between the Go binary and the reference binary; report divergences with the triggering input, expected output (reference), and actual output (Go binary)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support configurable normalization hooks that transform stdout and stderr before comparison, enabling known acceptable differences (e.g., timestamps, absolute paths) to pass\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go, named after the primary exported type DiffTest -- pkg/testutils/testutils.go is forbidden per project file-naming convention\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Default comparison mode is byte-for-byte on stdout and stderr, per ARCHITECTURE.yaml pkg/testutils component description\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Normalization hooks are functions applied to binary output before byte comparison, per ARCHITECTURE.yaml pkg/testutils normalization capability\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"DiffTest struct is exported and contains all fields specified in the PRD\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"The differential runner executes both binaries with identical inputs and returns a structured comparison result\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"When outputs diverge, the failure message includes the input arguments, expected output, and actual output\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/ succeeds with no compilation errors\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22279,"cache_read_input_tokens":19285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22279},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33aa31bd-9b3b-41c0-880e-3e12e5d4cde9","uuid":"4cd9033d-20af-4ba3-9009-9a94c31833f9"}
